# Notification service API
#
# @direct   -> the service itself, normally http://localhost:8082
#              (inside compose: http://notification:8082)
# @viaNginx -> through the frontend nginx proxy, http://localhost:8090
#
# The browser should only use @viaNginx.
# The backend calls @direct from inside the compose network.
#
# SSE is easier to watch with curl because most editors buffer the response:
#
#   curl -N http://localhost:8090/api/notification/stream
#
# Note the trailing slash on the collection URLs. /api/notification is the
# servlet context root, and Tomcat answers that with a 302 to
# /api/notification/ — redirects turn a POST into a GET, so writes silently
# do nothing. Always use {{direct}}/ and {{viaNginx}}/ for list/create.

@direct = http://localhost:8082/api/notification
@viaNginx = http://localhost:8090/api/notification

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### Health
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### Health check (direct, used by the container healthcheck)
GET {{direct}}/health

### Health check through nginx
GET {{viaNginx}}/health

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### History
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### List notifications, newest first (through nginx)
GET {{viaNginx}}/

### List notifications, newest first (direct)
GET {{direct}}/

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### Create notifications
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### Order created — this is the payload the backend sends
POST {{direct}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Order ORD-1002 was created for Alice (2 x 27-inch Monitor)",
  "entityId": 42,
  "notificationType": "ORDER_CREATED",
  "notificationLevel": "SUCCESS"
}

### Order shipped
POST {{direct}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Order ORD-1002 is now SHIPPED",
  "entityId": 42,
  "notificationType": "ORDER_SHIPPED",
  "notificationLevel": "INFO"
}

### Generic notification — useful for testing from the browser or curl
POST {{viaNginx}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Maintenance starts in 10 minutes",
  "entityId": 0,
  "notificationType": "GENERAL",
  "notificationLevel": "WARNING"
}

### Invalid request — expected 400 because message is blank
POST {{direct}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "   ",
  "entityId": 42,
  "notificationType": "GENERAL",
  "notificationLevel": "INFO"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### Delete
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### Delete a notification by id — expected 204 No Content
DELETE {{viaNginx}}/1

### Delete a missing id — expected 400 with "No resource found with id"
DELETE {{direct}}/999999

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### SSE stream
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### Live stream (direct)
# Use curl -N in a terminal:
#   curl -N http://localhost:8082/api/notification/stream
GET {{direct}}/stream
Accept: text/event-stream

### Live stream (through nginx)
# Use curl -N in a terminal:
#   curl -N http://localhost:8090/api/notification/stream
GET {{viaNginx}}/stream
Accept: text/event-stream
